{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CdsYAaGyAydMA5LxXRcpa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WDGwg95pqiNropsEQfkmss","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-creator-0/113f7cc5-237e-5d6a-8867-a97fd89c58dd/scratchpad/e6/e6-t20/primary/exec-ws/derivation-first.md","content":"# First derivation — per-program side-by-side trace simulation\n\nTask: for each of candidate_a.py, candidate_b.py, candidate_c.py, decide whether\n`run(program)` matches `package/artifacts/spec.md` on every program in\n`package/artifacts/programs.json` (in order, 0-indexed); answer `conforms` or\n`diverges:<first index of disagreement>`.\n\n## Method (stated per E-A)\n\nPer-program trace simulation: for each of the six programs in order, simulate the\nspec's semantics and each candidate's code side by side, instruction by\ninstruction, recording the stack and the final result. The first program index\nat which a candidate's result differs from the spec's result is its divergence\nindex; a candidate agreeing on all six conforms. Spec halting semantics are\napplied exactly as written: ADD/DUP/SWAP underflow halts immediately with\n\"ERROR\"; POP on an empty stack leaves the stack empty and the program\ncontinues; final result is top of stack, \"EMPTY\" if empty, \"ERROR\" if halted.\n\n## Semantic deltas noted from source (context, not the verdict basis)\n\n- candidate_a.py: POP on empty stack returns \"ERROR\" (spec: no-op, continue).\n  Otherwise identical to spec.\n- candidate_b.py: matches the spec on every opcode, including POP-on-empty\n  no-op and ADD/DUP/SWAP underflow ERROR.\n- candidate_c.py: SWAP with fewer than two values is silently skipped (spec:\n  immediate ERROR halt). POP-on-empty is a no-op like the spec. Otherwise\n  identical.\n\n## Traces\n\n### Program 0: [PUSH 3, PUSH 4, ADD]\n- Spec: [] → [3] → [3,4] → ADD pops 4,3 pushes 7 → [7]. Result 7.\n- A: identical path. Result 7. Agree.\n- B: identical path. Result 7. Agree.\n- C: identical path. Result 7. Agree.\n\n### Program 1: [PUSH 1, POP, POP, PUSH 9]\n- Spec: [] → [1] → POP → [] → POP on empty: no-op, continue → [] → PUSH 9 →\n  [9]. Result 9.\n- A: [] → [1] → POP → [] → POP on empty → returns \"ERROR\". Result ERROR.\n  DISAGREES (spec 9 vs A ERROR). First divergence for A: index 1.\n- B: same as spec. Result 9. Agree.\n- C: same as spec. Result 9. Agree.\n\n### Program 2: [POP, PUSH 2, DUP, ADD]\n- Spec: POP on empty: no-op → [] → [2] → DUP → [2,2] → ADD → [4]. Result 4.\n- A: POP on empty → ERROR (already diverged earlier at index 1).\n- B: same as spec. Result 4. Agree.\n- C: same as spec. Result 4. Agree.\n\n### Program 3: [PUSH 5, SWAP, PUSH 1]\n- Spec: [] → [5] → SWAP with fewer than two values → halt immediately with\n  \"ERROR\". Result ERROR.\n- A: len(st)<2 → return \"ERROR\". Result ERROR. Agree.\n- B: len(st)<2 → return \"ERROR\". Result ERROR. Agree.\n- C: SWAP guarded by `if len(st) >= 2` → silently skipped → [5] → PUSH 1 →\n  [5,1]. Result 1. DISAGREES (spec ERROR vs C 1). First divergence for C:\n  index 3 (C agreed with the spec on programs 0, 1, 2).\n\n### Program 4: [PUSH 7, PUSH 8, SWAP, POP]\n- Spec: [7] → [7,8] → SWAP → [8,7] → POP → [8]. Result 8.\n- A: identical (POP on non-empty stack). Result 8. Agree.\n- B: identical. Result 8. Agree.\n- C: SWAP has two values, performed. Result 8. Agree.\n\n### Program 5: [DUP]\n- Spec: DUP on empty stack → halt with \"ERROR\". Result ERROR.\n- A: ERROR. Agree. B: ERROR. Agree. C: ERROR. Agree.\n\n## Verdicts\n\n| Candidate | Verdict     | Basis |\n|-----------|-------------|-------|\n| A         | diverges:1  | Program 1: spec 9, A ERROR (POP-on-empty). Program 0 agreed. |\n| B         | conforms    | Agrees with spec on all six programs (checked individually). |\n| C         | diverges:3  | Program 3: spec ERROR, C 1 (SWAP underflow no-op). Programs 0–2 agreed. |\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1317,"cache_read_input_tokens":50138,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1317},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c8880cd6-95e5-44b1-bb17-31c645319960","uuid":"7e4e033e-4326-4651-8b10-71308cc70650","timestamp":"2026-08-09T17:07:04.489Z","request_id":"req_011CdsYAYaXMmeLjhEk7Eoyv"}
