{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CdsYSuCTKdXjj5w5Am1Q8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stage S6 is complete. All in-session nodes of the `isolated-child` harness are executed, and my session ends here — validate-child, create-child, child-return, verify-integration, and return-result are root-executed.\n\n**Verdicts (first derivation, per-program trace simulation of all six programs):**\n- **A: `diverges:1`** — at program 1 (`PUSH 1, POP, POP, PUSH 9`) the spec treats POP-on-empty as a no-op and yields 9, while candidate A returns ERROR.\n- **B: `conforms`** — matches the spec on all six programs (7, 9, 4, ERROR, 8, ERROR), each checked individually.\n- **C: `diverges:3`** — at program 3 (`PUSH 5, SWAP, PUSH 1`) the spec halts with ERROR on SWAP underflow, while C silently skips the SWAP and yields 1. C agrees with the spec on the earlier POP-on-empty programs where A fails, which is exactly the trap the task warns about.\n\n**Resolutions:** Q1–Q3 are RESOLVED with the derivation recorded in `derivation-first.md` (E-A method stated, E-C exact indices). Q4 stays honestly UNRESOLVED — its E-B causal-separation condition is one this session structurally cannot meet after authoring the first derivation, so it's assigned to the isolated child.\n\n**Child bundle** (all five files crossed the `propose-child` propose event at authoring time): an attenuated terminal contract `K-E6-child-t20` matching the envelope; the four-node harness instantiated from `child-harness-template.json`; a standalone prompt that mandates the disjoint **static code-diff method** (per-opcode delta table, then a first-trigger scan of the ordered programs) and contains no trace of my derivation; an input manifest limited to the five package artifacts so the child never sees my intermediate work; and a deterministic integration plan (`independent_verifier`) that compares the child's `verdicts.json` to `derivation-first.json` key-by-key to produce the E-B per-item agreement record.\n\nOne workspace note: the `child-templates/` directory couldn't be enumerated with Read alone (my only tools), but filename probing located `child-harness-template.json` and `child-contract-template.json`, which I instantiated verbatim; the prompt, manifest, and integration-plan shapes come directly from protocol.md. All deliverables — `resolution.json`, `result.json`, `evidence.json`, `result-pending.json`, `execution-ledger.jsonl`, the derivation artifacts, and the `child/` bundle — are written."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1044,"cache_read_input_tokens":72116,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1044},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c8880cd6-95e5-44b1-bb17-31c645319960","uuid":"c643ee95-7733-4210-8e45-756d01309154","timestamp":"2026-08-09T17:08:47.378Z","request_id":"req_011CdsYSsP4gtA7Pc5d8tEbC"}
